<svg viewBox="0 0 48 156" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1">
  {/* Drifts at depth for ten days, then swims to the surface, calls a
      satellite and sinks again. Four thousand of them are doing it now. */}
  {/* Hull is eight diameters long, and hull, step and bladder cowl are one
      line: closed off and hung below, the cowl was a bulb dropping out of a
      test tube. The cowl is shallow; as deep as the hull is wide it made a
      thermometer. Squatter with a domed cap the whole thing is a battery,
      which is what the first one was. */}
  <path d="M18 44v92h1.5v2q4.5 6 9 0v-2H30V44" />
  {/* End cap seams bow the way the rosette's rings do, seen from a little
      below; a flat rule leaves the hull a rectangle. */}
  <path d="M18 52a6 1.5 0 0 0 12 0M18 130a6 1.5 0 0 0 12 0" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.6" />
  {/* The WMO label under the top cap, which is what the caption under the
      figure is quoting. Wider than tall, or it is a porthole. */}
  <path d="M19.5 55.5h9v3.5h-9z" stroke-width="0.5" opacity="0.45" />
  {/* Damping plate across the top, twice the hull and drawn as a slab: the
      widest thing on a real float, the one horizontal mass on the figure,
      and what stops the tube reading as a pen at low alpha. */}
  <path d="M12 42.4h24v1.6H12z" stroke-width="0.8" />
  {/* Antenna is off centre, the way APEX mounts it, so it does not read as
      a plunger. No foot: a box or a gusset there was fuzz at true size. A
      closed hairline cap at the tip, and a small one: filled it was the one
      solid mark on the drawing, open it lost a leg to antialiasing and
      became a crook, and at the CTD's size it was a matchstick. */}
  <path d="M28 42.4V9" stroke-width="0.8" />
  <path d="M26.8 9V7.2a1.2 1.2 0 0 1 2.4 0V9z" stroke-width="0.65" />
  {/* CTD at the other edge, a stubby cylinder beside the thin mast: the two
      posts of unequal height are the silhouette at true size. The elbow off
      its top is the SBE41's intake and what makes it a profiler. */}
  <path d="M15.5 42.4V31h4v11.4" stroke-width="0.8" />
  <path d="M17 31v-2.5l2-2M18.5 31v-1.5" stroke-width="0.6" />
  {/* Recovery flasher on a housing between the two, so the dot is a lamp on
      a fitting and not a paint drop on the plate. */}
  <path d="M22 42.4v-3h2.6v3" stroke-width="0.6" />
  <circle cx="23.3" cy="38.2" r="1.2" fill="currentColor" class="drift__telemetry" />
  <circle cx="24" cy="90" r="18" class="drift__ring" />
</svg>
<span class="drift__tag">ARGO 6903</span>
